WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:02.650
sometimes we have to wonder and speculate

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:08.660
how someone comes to hold radical beliefs
or becomes motivated to commit violence in

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:09.740
the real world.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:14.519
And sometimes the people who do those things
will actually tell us and we've actually figured

00:00:14.519 --> 00:00:16.260
that out with the mag of bomber.

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:21.390
The Mag Obama is this 57 year old Florida
man who sent all those a pipe bombs through

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:24.020
the mail to Democrats and was ultimately caught.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:29.710
You'll remember maybe images of his van covered
in right wing messaging and stickers and he

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:35.280
has told us that he was radicalized by Fox
News along with other right wing media.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:40.160
He pled guilty to 65 counts back in March
and there's a whole bunch of court documents

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:44.820
that have now been released that are extremely
insightful as well as disturbing to be quite

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:49.690
honest with you and his attorney actually
said his attorneys say through these court

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:56.729
documents that the Mag Obama quote found light
in Donald Trump that he watched fox news quote

00:00:56.729 --> 00:01:02.100
religiously and specifically he was watching
Fox and friends in the morning and Hannity

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.100
in the evening.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.220
Check out this quote from the court documents.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:09.610
His infatuation with the president began as
something personal, not political when he

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:10.730
was most down.

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:14.780
Mr Siack relied on self help books on tape
to keep going.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:18.880
Donald Trump's books on success and business
were his favorites.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:23.810
Mr [inaudible] was an ardent Trump fan, and
when Trump announced he was running for president,

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:26.540
Mr [inaudible] enthusiastically supported
him.

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:31.640
He began watching Fox News religiously at
the gym, planning his morning workout to coincide

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:34.000
with Fox and friends and his evenings.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.780
To dovetail with Hannity.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:41.610
He became obsessed with quote attacks from
those he perceived as Trump's enemies.

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:45.860
And the court documents go on to outline that
he was not only radicalized through right

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:51.310
wing media and the Internet, but he used that
same internet to also learn to build the pipe

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:57.120
bombs that he ultimately ended up sending
to Hillary Clinton and Barack Obama, George

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:00.680
Soros, and a number of other people whose
names escape me.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:05.270
So the real important takeaway here is that
the media stuff is not a game.

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:09.340
Once you understand the concept of stochastic
terrorism, which I've talked about enough

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:13.430
this week, I'm not going to redefine it, but
Google it or check out some of my stories

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:15.190
from earlier this week about it.

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:21.560
When you understand the sort of fundamental
vulnerability of so many people, you really

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:26.560
should have a sense of responsibility for
everything that you say in a public forum,

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:32.030
in media, on TV or in a youtube channel, and
the radicalizing impact of extremist media

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:36.530
is just massive and if you won't listen to
live calls on our show, we've received a lot

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:41.790
of calls from people who call in and say they
were radicalized by, you know, they will sometimes

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:46.209
say it was Alex Jones or info wars, Stefan
Molyneux.

00:02:46.209 --> 00:02:49.100
Breitbart could be Fox News, could be the
blaze.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:50.780
There are less well known ones as well.

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:53.120
I can't think of all of them off hand.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:56.910
The point is, this is not an exception to
the rule.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:03:04.290
The combination of extremely outrageous content
meant to foment anger rather than activism

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:08.410
that benefits the majority of people or that
improve society.

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:17.440
This anger porn that is so popular among particularly
right wing media combined with the echo chamber,

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:23.100
algorithmic, a self perpetuating loops that
people can get into on youtube or another

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:25.850
places, online, Twitter, Facebook, et cetera.

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:31.750
This is meant to give people more and more
of what resonates with them the most and what

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:38.490
we have to understand is that for many people
that self, that constant feedback loop is

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:40.990
going to lead them to take real world action.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:46.430
This is not me saying, you know, Facebook's
algorithm is a terroristic, I'm not saying

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:47.430
that.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:48.430
I'm not going that far.

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:52.050
I'm not saying that when Glenn Beck rants
and raves about the tides foundation and someone

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:56.930
goes and tries to shoot up the ties foundation
that now Glen Beck is specifically guilty

00:03:56.930 --> 00:03:57.930
of a crime.

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:01.260
What I'm saying is if we want to have an adult
conversation that goes beyond the letter of

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:04.680
the law, we have to understand the responsibility
that we have.

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:08.400
Anytime people are consuming messages that
we put out into the media where you don't

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:09.720
know everyone that's hearing it, right?

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:14.200
When you're at a dinner party and you're talking
to six people, you know who is receiving your

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:20.049
message and you can in real time sort of gauge
their reaction and most people would naturally

00:04:20.049 --> 00:04:24.340
kind of tailor their speech to make sense
for the people that they're speaking to.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:29.190
When I do a segment and 500,000 people watch
it on Youtube, I don't know the mental state

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:30.419
of everybody who's watching.

00:04:30.419 --> 00:04:34.250
I don't know the way that everybody is hearing
what I'm saying.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:41.410
And I take that as a very serious responsibility
to try to speak in a way that is responsible

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:48.680
for, to use that same word, that type of responsibility
is something that seems completely missing

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:52.590
from a lot of these narratives that are crafted
by right wing media and these court documents

00:04:52.590 --> 00:05:15.970
tell us exactly 
how

00:05:15.970 --> 00:06:07.610
it works.

